; __autoOutput__ — per-block auto-output, and the fixture that makes it gateable.
;
; It is a PRIM rather than a source-level helper because "is this Unit?" is a runtime fact whose
; representation differs per backend, so every generator consuming F's output must implement it.
; Two of them did not: v2-jvm died with `unknown prim1: __autoOutput__` and v2-rust panicked with
; `unimplemented prim: __autoOutput__` — on EVERY program, so those lanes could not run anything.
; (v2/BUGS.md v2-source-backends-miss-autoOutput.)
;
; NO EXISTING FIXTURE USED THIS PRIM, which is why check.sh — a harness that otherwise compares
; every generator against the VM byte-for-byte — was green while two lanes were dead. That is the
; point of this file.
;
; Four cases, and the last two are the ones a careless implementation gets wrong:
;   1. an Int   -> printed
;   2. Unit     -> prints NOTHING and yields unit (the arm that makes it "auto")
;   3. a String -> printed RAW, not quoted. The generators' own `show` quotes strings; the VM's
;                  `out` does not, and byte-identical is byte-identical.
;   4. nested   -> the value of the whole seq is the LAST autoOutput's unit, so nothing extra prints.
;
; Expected output, from the VM:
;   7
;   hi
;   42
(program
 (defs
  (def main
   (lam 0
    (seq
     (prim __autoOutput__ (lit (int 7)))
     (seq
      (prim __autoOutput__ (lit unit))
      (seq
       (prim __autoOutput__ (lit (str "hi")))
       (prim __autoOutput__ (lit (int 42)))))))))
 (entry (app (global main))))
